<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss, U.S. reach accord on public procurement.</title>
<headline>Swiss, U.S. reach accord on public procurement.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland and the United States have concluded a bilateral trade accord that liberalises mutual access to government procurement contracts, the U.S. embassy in Berne said on Monday.</p>
<p>The accord, which must still be ratified by the Swiss parliament, follows similar deals between the United States and Japan, the European Union and Norway, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave no details, and officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
